-    token is not touched: "Nan Goldin" is safe unless the node itself asserts
-    given "Nan" AND family "Goldin", and even then only if a better name exists.
-  - If the repair cannot find a BETTER name, it leaves the node alone and says
-    so. Rewriting to something no more correct is churn on real data.
-
-TWO KINDS OF REPAIR, AND THEY ARE NOT APPROVED TOGETHER
-  full name   the node also holds a real given name, so the repair RECOVERS
-              information already on the node: "Mum Smith" -> "Jane Smith".
-              Done by --apply.
-  mononym     the only given name IS the kinship word, so the only available
-              replacement is the family name alone: "Mum Smith" -> "Smith".
